			"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriskirknielsen/114077790888610828",
			"author": {
				"name": "Christopher Kirk-Nielsen",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriskirknielsen",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/112/011/424/167/261/417/original/b7483cef1bc6d1dd.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-27T20:42:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Silly question (out of curiosity, not anything I am dead-set on figuring out): for the Google Dev site, the favicon is evenly (ish) spread across 4 colours, but the output is yellow. I didn't look too much at the code (sorry) but is there a magic thing that determines which hue \"wins\"?</p><p>Also, gotta say this is very cool! It fits neatly in the \"Whimsy\" and \"Surprise &amp; Delight\" Venn diagram. (as overused as that second term may be these days 😅)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114078172628184225",
			"parentId": "114077133668297255",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@uncenter/114078172613914416",
			"author": {
				"name": "uncenter",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@uncenter",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/792/094/176/764/079/original/ef375a085dcf85d5.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-27T22:19:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> i also think we could decouple that from eleventy since it bears little relation- i do think that relation to eleventy should matter in terms of namespacing.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114078300483119422",
			"parentId": "114078172628184225",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114078300483119422",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-27T22:52:03.681Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@uncenter\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>uncenter</span></a></span> I think there are four different styles at play here, which do you mean?</p><p>1. @11ty/eleventy-plugin-UTIL<br />2. @11ty/eleventy-UTIL<br />3. @11ty/UTIL<br />4. UTIL</p><p>I agree that #2 *could* go away (though renaming packages is annoying enough for folks that I don’t think it’s worth it, unless there is a larger issue)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114082231713580442",
